# Phaser Audio Management Best Practices

## Context
- When implementing sound effects and music in Phaser games
- When targeting multiple platforms with different audio capabilities
- When implementing dynamic or adaptive audio in Phaser
- When optimizing audio performance for mobile devices
- When creating games requiring complex audio layering, mixing, or transitions

## Requirements
- Configure Phaser's sound manager with optimal parameters during game initialization
- Use Phaser's built-in audio pooling and audio sprites for performance optimization
- Implement a centralized audio manager class to handle all Phaser audio interactions
- Properly preload all audio assets in Phaser's loading scene with multiple formats
- Implement efficient clean-up of audio resources during scene transitions
- Apply sound rate limiting and prioritization for high-action gameplay
- Use Phaser's WebAudio capabilities for spatial audio and advanced effects

