## Phaser Audio Implementation Best Practices

### 1. Configure Phaser's Sound Manager Optimally

```typescript
// In your game config
const config: Phaser.Types.Core.GameConfig = {
  // ... other config
  audio: {
    disableWebAudio: false,  // Use WebAudio API for better performance
    noAudio: false,          // Only set true for debugging
    context: null,           // Let Phaser create its own context
    disableAudio: false      // Enable audio
  }
};

// In your scene's create method
create() {
  // Configure global sound options
  this.sound.setVolume(1.0);
  this.sound.setRate(1.0);
  
  // On mobile, limit concurrent sounds
  if (this.sys.game.device.os.android || this.sys.game.device.os.iOS) {
    this.sound.setMaxListeners(8);
  }
}
```

### 2. Use Audio Sprites for Small Effects

```typescript
// Load audio sprite in preload
preload() {
  this.load.audioSprite('sfx', 
    'assets/audio/sfx.json',
    ['assets/audio/sfx.ogg', 'assets/audio/sfx.mp3']
  );
}

// Create and use the sprite
create() {
  // Add the audio sprite once
  this.sfx = this.sound.addAudioSprite('sfx');
}

// Play different markers from the same sprite
playCoin() {
  this.sfx.play('coin');
}

playJump() {
  this.sfx.play('jump');
